<title>USA: KOCH raises U.S. posted crude prices 25 cts/bbl.</title>
<headline>KOCH raises U.S. posted crude prices 25 cts/bbl.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Koch Oil said it had raised the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 25 cents, effective Friday.</p>
<p>The decrease brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $20.50 a barrel and West Texas Sour to $18.25 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $20.50 and Oklahoma sweet is $20.50.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1620</p>
</text>
